 "diagnosis": {
  "codex_1447": "OVERLAP=0: the hbm side takes the next descriptor only after the whole block has RETURNED (desc_rd_ready=!h_active), so every block pays the full ~150 ns fill latency serially; DECOUPLE=0: a landing bank can only be re-reserved after the SAME-index cache bank retired (reserve_ready required !cache_owned)",
  "fix_h_die": "OVERLAP=1 (ot_hbm_svc_prefetch_overlap_owner + per-bank return counters: next block issues once every owner has issued; responses carry bank/epoch per tag) + DECOUPLE=1 (cache ownership checked at open/start, where packed136 already faults an open into an owned bank): 139.3 -> 108.9 ns/epoch",
  "remaining": "none at the service stage for 64-row blocks: PC-peak limited",
  "fix_lbanks4": "LBANKS=4 (default): four 64-row landing blocks per landing bank in one actual ot_sram_1r1w_256x256_m2_r2c2 (2-bit landing index; cache bank = landing index LSB): 69.58 ns/epoch = 104.2 B/cycle/SM = 1.053 x price, now limited by the four-PC transfer floor (68 sectors/PC x 1.024 ns = 69.6 ns)"
 },
